 "instruction": "Extend the cognitive-rate controller (`sanctuary/core/cycle_rate.py`) with asymmetric smoothing and a turbo mode, and let the entity propose its own rate.\n\n**Constants** (all importable from `cycle_rate`):\n\n| Constant | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `MIN_RATE_HZ` | 0.05 |\n| `SLIDER_MAX_HZ` | 10.0 |\n| `TURBO_DEFAULT_HZ` | 60.0 |\n| `TURBO_MAX_HZ` | 100.0 |\n| `MAX_RATE_HZ` | `TURBO_MAX_HZ` (the substrate ceiling) |\n| `DEFAULT_SLOWDOWN_SECONDS` | 20.0 |\n| `DEFAULT_SPEEDUP_SECONDS` | 0.5 |\n\nAlso add a very short turbo snap window, `TURBO_SNAP_SECONDS = 0.05`.\n\n**`CycleRateController(initial_hz=SLIDER_MAX_HZ, slowdown_seconds=DEFAULT_SLOWDOWN_SECONDS, speedup_seconds=DEFAULT_SPEEDUP_SECONDS)`.** This replaces the old single `smoothing_seconds` argument.\n- Expose `slowdown_seconds` and `speedup_seconds` properties.\n- **Clamping.** Rates are clamped to `[MIN_RATE_HZ, MAX_RATE_HZ]`, so a proposal of 50 Hz is accepted.\n- **Smoothing.** `propose_rate` picks its window by direction: `slowdown_seconds` when the target is below the current rate, `speedup_seconds` otherwise.\n  - `tick(elapsed)` eases linearly from where the rate was at the proposal to the target over that window.\n  - A zero window snaps on any tick.\n  - A non-positive elapsed does nothing.\n  - A controller is settled at construction.\n- **Turbo engage.** `engage_turbo(target_hz=TURBO_DEFAULT_HZ)`:\n  - Remembers the current non-turbo target. Engaging again while turbo is active keeps the original remembered target.\n  - Sets `is_turbo_active`.\n  - Records a proposal with source `\"turbo\"` and snaps using `TURBO_SNAP_SECONDS`.\n- **Turbo release.** `release_turbo()`:\n  - Does nothing when turbo isn't active.\n  - Otherwise clears turbo and returns to the remembered target using the slowdown window, with source `\"turbo_release\"`.\n- **Turbo duration.** `turbo_duration_seconds` is the time since turbo engaged (monotonic clock), or 0.0 when inactive.\n- **History.** Every proposal, including turbo ones, appears in `proposal_history` (a copy); `RateProposal` gains a `timestamp`.\n- **Slider clamp.** Add a module function `clamp_to_slider(rate_hz)` that clamps to `[MIN_RATE_HZ, SLIDER_MAX_HZ]`.\n\n**Entity proposals:**\n- In `sanctuary/core/schema.py`, add a Pydantic model `CycleRateProposal` with `target_hz: float` (validated to `ge=0.05, le=10.0`) and `anticipatory: bool = False`.\n- Add `CognitiveOutput.cycle_rate_proposal: Optional[CycleRateProposal] = None`.\n- In `CognitiveCycle` (`sanctuary/core/cognitive_cycle.py`), after scaffold integration, when an output carries a proposal, call `rate_controller.propose_rate(clamp_to_slider(target_hz), source=\"entity\", anticipatory=...)`. Log and swallow any error; it must never break the cycle.",
